            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThere is not much that can be done here. Base16 has only 4 shades of background colors and 4 shades of foreground colors (or more like 2, because base06 and base07 are usually hardly distinguishable from white).\r\n\r\nHighlight group for current tab [has regular foreground with visible background](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/78cf17f23dd5372154e1cc90dc3ae27da6368742/lua/mini/base16.lua#L715), while all highlight groups for modified tabs [use forground/background colors for background/foreground](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/78cf17f23dd5372154e1cc90dc3ae27da6368742/lua/mini/base16.lua#L718-L720) to make them stand out.\r\n\r\nThe reason you are not seeing much contrast is likely because there is not much contrast between light background (base01, base02) and dark foreground (base04).\r\n\r\nI can suggest at least the following:\r\n- Tweak those base background/foreground colors for more contrast.\r\n- Redefine highlight groups of 'mini.tabline' to your liking after loading 'mini.base16'.\r\n\r\nClosing as not a bug.",
            "created_at": "2023-07-21T07:16:35Z",
